# `just fmt` runs `prettier --write .` over the whole repository, and
# `just fmt-check` runs `prettier --check .` over it. Every entry below is a
# file prettier CAN parse and MUST NOT rewrite, with the reason it must not.
# Anything prettier cannot parse at all (`.rs`, `.sql`, `.sha256`, `.cstack`)
# is never selected in the first place and needs no entry — except where an
# entry is the guarantee rather than an observation, which is said so below.
#
# Prettier 3 reads `.gitignore` as well as this file, so generated trees
# (`dist/`, `storybook-static/`, `.e2e/`, `node_modules/`) are already out of
# scope and are deliberately not repeated here.
#
# THERE IS A SECOND IGNORE FILE: `examples/shop/.prettierignore`, for the
# `zen generate` output and `.next/`. It applies to that package's own `lint`
# script (`prettier --check`, run from that directory) and NOT to `just fmt`
# or `just fmt-check-web`, which run from here and read only this file. The
# two agree today, measured rather than assumed: every path it names is
# either in the root `.gitignore` already or a file prettier cannot parse
# (`examples/shop/zenstack/migrations/` holds `.sql` and a `.toml`, and
# `schema.zmodel` is not a language prettier knows). Add a `.ts`, `.json` or
# `.md` under one of those paths and they stop agreeing — the root run would
# check a generated file the package deliberately excludes. Mirror the entry
# here if that happens.

# Helm templates are Go templates that happen to have a `.yaml` extension: a
# line like `{{- include "vpay.validate" . -}}` is not YAML, prettier's YAML
# parser rejects it, and anything it did manage to reformat would break the
# indentation the templates depend on. `helm lint` is the formatter for this
# directory.
deploy/helm/**/templates/

# Fixture for
# `a_malformed_yaml_file_produces_a_clean_typed_error_not_a_panic`
# (`backends/crates/vpay-config/tests/fixtures/`). The unterminated quote is a
# genuine YAML syntax error: prettier cannot parse it, so `--write` leaves it
# alone but `--check` exits non-zero on it. That is the exp17 hazard
# (docs/plans/exp17-notes/opus-review.md finding 2), and the reason
# `just fmt-check` could not run prettier until this entry existed.
backends/crates/vpay-config/tests/fixtures/malformed.yml

# Generated by pnpm, in pnpm's own layout, and rewritten by pnpm on every
# install that resolves anything. Prettier's YAML printer produces a
# semantically identical but textually different file (measured 2026-09-10:
# +5444/-2837 lines, byte-different, parse-identical), so formatting it buys
# nothing and costs two things: `just fmt` stops being a no-op the moment
# anyone adds a dependency, and every dependency PR carries an eight-thousand
# line reformat that conflicts with every other branch in flight.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# `sqlx::migrate!` checksums the bytes of each migration, and
# `backends/migrations/MANIFEST.sha256` pins those checksums
# (`just verify-migrations`). A reflowed comment in a migration that has
# already shipped stops every database that applied the original from booting
# (issue #76, docs/runbooks/migrations.md). Prettier has no SQL parser today,
# so this entry changes nothing right now — it is here so the guarantee
# survives prettier gaining one, or someone adding a SQL plugin.
# `backends/migrations/README.md` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is prose,
# nothing hashes it, and it is already prettier-clean.
backends/migrations/*.sql

# Flutter/Dart tooling output (`sdks/flutter/*/build/`, `.dart_tool/`).
# Unlike every other generated tree named at the top of this file, these are
# NOT covered by the root `.gitignore`: git ignores them through the package's
# own nested file (`sdks/flutter/vpay_checkout_flutter/.gitignore`), and
# prettier reads only the ROOT `.gitignore`. So the "already out of scope"
# sentence above does not reach them, and an entry here is the guarantee
# rather than an observation.
#
# Measured 2026-09-14: after a `flutter test` and a `flutter build apk`,
# `just fmt-check-web` reported style issues in 150 files, of which 139 were
# generated JSON/manifests under these two trees and 12 were real source.
# CI never sees them — it runs no Flutter recipe (D-M3) — so this is a local
# papercut, not a CI failure, and it is real for anyone who builds the plugin.
sdks/flutter/**/build/
sdks/flutter/**/.dart_tool/

# Agent worktrees (`.claude/worktrees/<name>/`), for the same reason as the
# Flutter trees above and with the same consequence: git does not ignore
# `.claude/` — `.claude/skills/vaam-ui` is tracked — so the root `.gitignore`
# does not put these out of scope, and each worktree is a FULL SECOND COPY of
# this repository. `prettier --check .` from the main checkout therefore walks
# every checked-out branch as well as this one, and the run grows with the
# number of worktrees rather than with the size of the tree.
#
# This is what made `just ci` time out in `fmt-check-web` on PR #172 while its
# author was verifying it. CI never sees it — a runner clones one tree and has
# no `.claude/worktrees/` — so it is a local papercut, not a CI failure, and
# it is real for anyone who uses `git worktree` under `.claude/`.
.claude/worktrees/
